<title>YEMEN: French minister in Yemen to increase investments.</title>
<headline>French minister in Yemen to increase investments.</headline>
<dateline>SANAA 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's minister of industry, post and telecommunications arrived in the Yemeni capital Sanaa on Monday and said his country sought to increase investments in the small independent oil-producing state.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a French desire to expand French investments in Yemen,&quot; Franck Borotra told the Yemeni news agency SABA.</p>
<p>The minister was accompanied by Thierry Desmaret, president of oil company Total, Edmond Alphandery, president of Electricite de France (EDF), and Denis Verret, vice-president of Aerospatiale.</p>
<p>Total has a 36 percent stake in a $5 billion foreign-backed liquefied natural gas project in Yemen. U.S. Exxon Corp jointly with Hunt oil holds 30 percent, South Korea's Yukong eight percent and the Yemeni government 26 percent.</p>
